00:22:32.690 --> 00:22:35.690
when an explosion destroyed your camp.

00:22:35.690 --> 00:22:37.690
And you were left for dead.

00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:40.690
Lex saved my life.

00:22:40.690 --> 00:22:41.690
I owe him everything.

00:22:41.690 --> 00:22:48.380
This is how a Luther rewards that kind of loyalty.

00:22:48.380 --> 00:22:49.380
What are you doing?

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:51.380
I'm opening your eyes.

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:02.500
There's a nanotransmitter hardwired to your optic nerve.

00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:06.500
You've been Lex's eyes and ears for quite some time.

00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:09.500
He's watching us right now.

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:22.740
Lex might have saved you,

00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:25.740
but he never trusted you, Ted.

00:23:25.740 --> 00:23:34.289
I'm sorry.

00:23:34.289 --> 00:23:50.890
I'll let you know as soon as Detective Jones wakes up.

00:23:50.890 --> 00:23:52.890
He's strong, but he's not out of the woods yet.

00:23:52.890 --> 00:23:53.890
Thank you, Doctor.

00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:55.890
Fordman.

00:23:55.890 --> 00:23:57.890
Look, take it easy.

00:23:57.890 --> 00:23:58.890
Take it easy?

00:23:58.890 --> 00:23:59.890
Come here.

00:23:59.890 --> 00:24:01.890
I saw you chatting up your buddy, the green arrow.

00:24:01.890 --> 00:24:04.890
He took down our whole squad and you just let him walk?

00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:05.890
Look, I don't know what you think you saw.

00:24:05.890 --> 00:24:07.890
All you do is ask questions about some detective,

00:24:07.890 --> 00:24:10.890
and then I find you checking up on him in the hospital too?

00:24:10.890 --> 00:24:13.890
Who are you, Joe? You fed? I-A-B?

00:24:13.890 --> 00:24:15.890
I want to take down the guy who shot him,

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:18.890
and I know that the shooter's a part of your squad.

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:20.890
They cross the line, Danny.

00:24:20.890 --> 00:24:23.890
This isn't the first time they've gone after somebody who slipped through this.

00:24:23.890 --> 00:24:24.890
system?

00:24:24.890 --> 00:24:25.890
Someone has to.

00:24:25.890 --> 00:24:26.890
What about John Jones?

00:24:26.890 --> 00:24:28.890
He was on to your little linch mob, wasn't he?

00:24:28.890 --> 00:24:32.650
Someone shot him to cover it up.

00:24:32.650 --> 00:24:36.150
Who are you protecting?

00:24:36.150 --> 00:24:38.150
You don't roll over on a badge, not ever.

00:24:38.150 --> 00:24:40.150
Then why is it okay to shoot one?

00:24:40.150 --> 00:24:44.140
Hey, these guys have my back.

00:24:44.140 --> 00:24:46.140
Well, it's just more than I can say for you.

00:24:46.140 --> 00:24:49.140
I do have your back, Danny, and I might be the only one.

00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:56.230
This is not justice.

00:24:56.230 --> 00:24:58.230
Joe, I'm just one man.

00:24:58.230 --> 00:25:00.230
What can one man do?

00:25:00.230 --> 00:25:05.500
Ask yourself while you put that uniform on in the first place.

00:25:05.500 --> 00:25:06.500
in the first place.

00:25:06.500 --> 00:25:32.200
Imagine my surprise when I stumbled upon Metropolis's finest going gangland.

00:25:32.200 --> 00:25:35.200
Thug's a really good look for you and your crew, by the way.

00:25:35.200 --> 00:25:37.200
They're not all bad, Oliver.

00:25:37.200 --> 00:25:41.200
Some of them are out there every day risking their lives and their families trying to do the same thing we own.

00:25:41.200 --> 00:25:43.200
Yeah, I'm sure you're right.

00:25:43.200 --> 00:25:47.200
You know, Alice forget, how many parolees did we rough up last month?

00:25:47.200 --> 00:25:48.200
Do you remember?

00:25:48.200 --> 00:25:52.200
Of all people, I thought you would understand that this isn't just black and white.

00:25:52.200 --> 00:25:55.200
No matter how noble their intentions when they started, Clark, these people have gone too far.

00:25:55.200 --> 00:25:56.200
too far.

00:25:56.200 --> 00:25:57.200
And you never have?

00:25:57.200 --> 00:26:02.220
Danny watched that guy kill his partner.

00:26:02.220 --> 00:26:07.220
Tell me you've never been tempted to look into eyes of someone who just committed so much pain

00:26:07.220 --> 00:26:10.069
and just...

00:26:10.069 --> 00:26:11.069
Kill him.

00:26:11.069 --> 00:26:12.069
Kill them.

00:26:12.069 --> 00:26:16.220
For the greater good? You're going to stand there and tell me that's what you believe?

00:26:16.220 --> 00:26:18.220
I didn't think so.

00:26:18.220 --> 00:26:21.220
What I'm saying is that saving someone, truly saving them,

00:26:21.220 --> 00:26:24.220
is not about knocking them out and throwing them in a dark room.

00:26:24.220 --> 00:26:27.220
It's about helping them find their way back to the right side.

00:26:27.220 --> 00:26:30.230
You know what, Clark?

00:26:30.230 --> 00:26:31.230
Some people are beyond saving.

00:26:31.230 --> 00:26:36.049
That's the suspect that Jones tracked down.

00:26:36.049 --> 00:26:38.049
He didn't find his way back to custody, Clark.

00:26:38.049 --> 00:26:41.049
He did, however, manage to find his way to the bottom of a river.

00:26:41.049 --> 00:26:43.049
Now, these cops are taking the law into their own hands.

00:26:43.049 --> 00:26:46.049
How many more people have to die before you do anything?

00:26:46.049 --> 00:26:48.049
All right, look, I have narrowed it down to Simmons and Talbot.

00:26:48.049 --> 00:26:50.049
Both have sniper training.

00:26:50.049 --> 00:26:53.049
Great. You sit here and you play detective.

00:26:53.049 --> 00:26:56.049
I'm going to go make sure your boys don't get a chance to put another person in the hospital.

00:26:56.049 --> 00:27:21.369
Samar.

00:27:21.369 --> 00:27:28.400
This is something you need to know about, Joe.

00:27:28.400 --> 00:27:30.400
I made a couple calls.

00:27:30.400 --> 00:27:31.400
He's not who he says.

00:27:31.400 --> 00:27:32.400
He's not who he says.

00:27:32.400 --> 00:28:08.119
he is.

00:28:08.119 --> 00:28:09.119
Should have called ahead.

00:28:09.119 --> 00:28:11.119
I would have had the white set of place at the table for you.

00:28:11.119 --> 00:28:14.119
Clark Kent, you're under arrest for the attempted murder to detect John Jones.

00:28:14.119 --> 00:28:25.750
You set me up?

00:28:25.750 --> 00:28:26.750
You better than this.

00:28:26.750 --> 00:28:45.299
You did the right thing.

00:28:45.299 --> 00:28:48.299
There's one loose thread to tie up.

00:28:48.299 --> 00:28:53.500
Your hands have been cleaned for way too long, Danny Boy.

00:28:53.500 --> 00:28:55.500
Hey, smile.

00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:58.500
You're going to be the man who killed the Green Arrow.

00:28:58.500 --> 00:29:24.819
This is messed up.

00:29:24.819 --> 00:29:26.819
You said you were transferring me.

00:29:26.819 --> 00:29:28.819
We're not going to kill you. You're just a bait.

00:29:28.819 --> 00:29:29.819
You're ready, Denny.

00:29:29.819 --> 00:29:35.470
How you know the arrow's gonna show?

00:29:35.470 --> 00:29:37.470
You can't help himself.

00:29:37.470 --> 00:29:41.470
After the other night, you can bet he's been watching us.

00:29:41.470 --> 00:29:56.460
I should do it.

00:29:56.460 --> 00:29:58.460
Let him have it.

00:29:58.460 --> 00:30:04.950
Showtime, kid.

00:30:04.950 --> 00:30:13.670
We gotta stop meeting like this.

00:30:13.670 --> 00:30:20.980
You're welcome.

00:30:20.980 --> 00:30:22.980
Damn it, Turpin, move in.

00:30:22.980 --> 00:30:25.980
Turn around. Show me your hands.

00:30:25.980 --> 00:30:33.069
It's not bad.

00:30:33.069 --> 00:30:35.069
It's not every day someone gets to drop on me.

00:30:35.069 --> 00:30:36.069
Is this all joke to you?

00:30:36.069 --> 00:30:37.069
To you?

00:30:37.069 --> 00:30:38.069
That guy took a shot at me.

00:30:38.069 --> 00:30:39.069
And you were gonna what?

00:30:39.069 --> 00:30:41.069
Put him in the ground?

00:30:41.069 --> 00:30:42.069
Damn, Turpin.

00:30:42.069 --> 00:30:43.069
You got the shot, take it.

00:30:43.069 --> 00:30:51.410
You're Joe's partner, right?

00:30:51.410 --> 00:30:53.410
His name is Clark Kent.

00:30:53.410 --> 00:30:55.410
This isn't about him, okay?

00:30:55.410 --> 00:30:57.410
Got the shot, Danny. Come on, take it.

00:30:57.410 --> 00:31:00.410
It's not too late for you. You don't have to do this.

00:31:00.410 --> 00:31:03.410
Why don't you case just mind your own damn business, huh?

00:31:03.410 --> 00:31:05.410
You don't know these guys like I do?

00:31:05.410 --> 00:31:07.410
I got a family at home.

00:31:07.410 --> 00:31:09.410
When your little boy asks you who you saved today,

00:31:09.410 --> 00:31:11.410
you can tell him you killed a man in cold blood.

00:31:11.410 --> 00:31:12.410
blood.

00:31:12.410 --> 00:31:13.410
It ain't like that.

00:31:13.410 --> 00:31:15.410
I knew you were a part of this.

00:31:15.410 --> 00:31:16.410
But Clark actually trusted you.

00:31:16.410 --> 00:31:18.410
He thinks you just lost your way.

00:31:18.410 --> 00:31:20.410
Take the shot, Danny.

00:31:20.410 --> 00:31:33.410
Man, if this is what you need to do, define yourself, then do it.

00:31:33.410 --> 00:31:35.410
You do it.

00:31:35.410 --> 00:31:38.410
You pull the trigger, you can prove Clark wrong.

00:31:38.410 --> 00:31:43.609
Real hero.

00:31:43.609 --> 00:31:45.609
Take the shot, Danny.

00:31:45.609 --> 00:32:15.509
Dispatch.

00:32:15.509 --> 00:32:18.509
Green Arrow is spotted on 16th Avenue, assaulting an officer.

00:32:18.509 --> 00:32:21.509
Requesting backup. Officer is Dell.

00:32:21.509 --> 00:32:31.799
How many times did I swear?

00:32:31.799 --> 00:32:33.799
Turpin wouldn't seal the deal.

00:32:33.799 --> 00:32:35.799
Pay up.

00:32:35.799 --> 00:33:14.430
Like you said, always wear a vest.

00:33:14.430 --> 00:34:00.720
One of the good guys.

00:34:00.720 --> 00:34:03.720
Feels good to be back on my feet again.

00:34:03.720 --> 00:34:06.720
I don't know how many favors you into call in.

00:34:06.720 --> 00:34:10.719
Thank you for getting me out of trouble with the police.

00:34:10.719 --> 00:34:12.719
It was the least I could do.

00:34:12.719 --> 00:34:13.719
Could have used some backup out there.

00:34:13.719 --> 00:34:15.719
some backup out there.

00:34:15.719 --> 00:34:17.719
Why didn't you call me in sooner?

00:34:17.719 --> 00:34:20.719
The same reason I've had to pull you from the brink of death before.

00:34:20.719 --> 00:34:25.280
Same reason you let your guard down last night.

00:34:25.280 --> 00:34:36.260
After knowing what it's like to truly feel powerful,

00:34:36.260 --> 00:34:40.260
to have the ability to change fate,

00:34:40.260 --> 00:34:43.989
it's hard to admit when you can't do it alone.

00:34:43.989 --> 00:34:49.360
I guess going solo is really caught up with this lately, Leon.

00:34:49.360 --> 00:34:56.139
You know, for everything Danny's crew did wrong, I have to say,

00:34:56.139 --> 00:34:59.139
knowing there's always someone there who has your back,

00:34:59.139 --> 00:35:03.780
The kind of brotherhood can make you feel like you could do anything.

00:35:03.780 --> 00:35:17.760
When I thought my life was over, you gave me a reason to keep going.

00:35:17.760 --> 00:35:23.090
It wouldn't be who I am without you.

00:35:23.090 --> 00:35:36.869
Because I respected you.

00:35:36.869 --> 00:35:39.869
I've done everything you've ever asked.

00:35:39.869 --> 00:35:42.869
You've seen that?

00:35:42.869 --> 00:35:44.869
With your own eyes?

00:35:44.869 --> 00:35:47.869
And apparently, with mine.

00:35:47.869 --> 00:35:59.420
I hope you watch with rapt attention,

00:35:59.420 --> 00:36:01.420
as your bank accounts close,

00:36:01.420 --> 00:36:02.420
as you lose all contact with the outside.

00:36:02.420 --> 00:36:09.420
contact with the outside world as your life disappears before your eyes.

00:36:09.420 --> 00:36:35.809
Goodbye, Lex. I loved you. You son.

00:36:35.809 --> 00:36:55.760
Mercy. Wow. I sure hope your smores are worth a drive.

00:36:55.760 --> 00:37:00.760
Wouldn't want you to spoil your appetite or going to dinner.

00:37:00.760 --> 00:37:02.760
I'd like to discuss a merger.

00:37:02.760 --> 00:37:09.579
Ha, ha. A merger. What kind of merger?

00:37:09.579 --> 00:37:15.219
Any kind you want. Don't keep me waiting.

00:37:15.219 --> 00:37:32.159
Alright, bud. It's PJ time, okay?

00:37:32.159 --> 00:37:41.550
Green Arrow?

00:37:41.550 --> 00:37:44.550
No. Robin Hood.

00:37:44.550 --> 00:37:47.550
You know, most people think he's a bad guy, but he isn't.

00:37:47.550 --> 00:37:50.550
Because that's what my kid tells me. Go figure.

00:37:50.550 --> 00:37:51.550
There's be all those bright colors.

00:37:51.550 --> 00:37:57.880
Danny, I'm sorry I couldn't tell you I was a reporter.

00:37:57.880 --> 00:38:01.880
Yeah, well, I can't really be mad at you, Clark.

00:38:01.880 --> 00:38:06.880
I want to be. But, uh, you're just doing what you felt was right.

00:38:06.880 --> 00:38:09.880
which is more than I can save for myself.

00:38:09.880 --> 00:38:14.880
I just got all turned around.

00:38:14.880 --> 00:38:17.880
I'm glad you found your way again.

00:38:17.880 --> 00:38:20.880
Yeah, well, let's hold off on that until the inquest next week.

00:38:20.880 --> 00:38:24.699
But no matter what happens,

00:38:24.699 --> 00:38:29.230
I know that they can be proud of me from now on.

00:38:29.230 --> 00:38:39.980
Hey, Danny, is it hard

00:38:39.980 --> 00:38:44.610
to put them through what you do every day?

00:38:44.610 --> 00:38:47.610
You just can't lose sight of the people you're trying to protect, you know?

00:38:47.610 --> 00:38:49.610
It'll be hard or not doing it.

00:38:49.610 --> 00:38:53.489
I do what I do what I do.

00:38:53.489 --> 00:39:09.219
I do just to keep them safe. What about you, Clark? You got someone who makes it all worth it?

00:39:09.219 --> 00:39:37.889
If I squint just right, it's like we're 14 again.

00:39:37.889 --> 00:39:41.199
You say that like it's a good thing.

00:39:41.199 --> 00:39:43.199
What's up?

00:39:43.199 --> 00:39:47.090
I couldn't sleep.

00:39:47.090 --> 00:39:53.780
So you came to a coffee shop? Not your best plan, Mr. Kent.

00:39:53.780 --> 00:40:04.349
Mauna, I know you had reasons for coming back. Why are you staying?

00:40:04.349 --> 00:40:06.349
Leaving's harder than I thought it would be.

00:40:06.349 --> 00:40:09.940
But like I said,

00:40:09.940 --> 00:40:12.940
Like I said, I don't know how long I'll be here, so.

00:40:12.940 --> 00:40:18.340
Whether you leave in 10 years or you leave tomorrow,

00:40:18.340 --> 00:40:20.340
the important thing is you're here today.

00:40:27.090 --> 00:40:29.090
We aren't 14 anymore.

00:40:29.090 --> 00:40:32.090
The world will always be bigger than the both of us.

00:40:32.090 --> 00:40:34.090
Maybe it doesn't have to be all or nothing.

00:40:34.090 --> 00:40:41.760
For the last year.

00:40:41.760 --> 00:40:44.760
All I've done is sacrifice myself

00:40:44.760 --> 00:40:46.760
and everything that I love for the greater good.

00:40:46.760 --> 00:40:56.380
What if the rest of the world didn't have to come first?

00:40:56.380 --> 00:40:59.380
The world needs you, Clark.

00:40:59.380 --> 00:41:00.380
What about what we need?

00:41:00.380 --> 00:41:01.380
What about what we need?

00:41:01.380 --> 00:41:03.380
Thank you.

